  {
    "id": "structured-logging-production",
    "title": "Structured Logging Saved My Production Debug Session",
    "excerpt": "3 AM. A recruitment sync is failing silently. Users are missing candidates. I have no idea where.",
    "content": "3 AM. A recruitment sync is failing silently. Users are missing candidates. I have no idea where.\n\nOld logging approach: print(f\"Processing job {job_id}\")\nProblem: trying to grep logs for a specific user's data is like finding a needle in a haystack while wearing mittens.\n\nSwitched to structured JSON logging. Changed everything.\n\nInstead of: Took 10 seconds to see: API returned 429 (rate limited), that's why sync stopped. Old logs? Would have taken 45 minutes.\n\nPattern:\n```python\nlogger.info(json.dumps({\n    \"trace_id\": trace_id,\n    \"task_id\": task_id,\n    \"step\": \"SEARCH\",\n    \"latency_ms\": latency,\n    \"tokens_used\": tokens,\n    \"status\": \"COMPLETED\"\n}))\n```\n\nThis is the difference between debugging blindfolded and having a spotlight.",
    "tags": [
      "DevOps",
      "Observability"
    ],
    "palette": "linear-gradient(135deg,#9b7bff,#ff5ea0)",
    "shape": "wave",
